  "generated_note": "Automated Friday run (2026-10-02) pulled live from Metricool per AUTOMATION.md, window Sep 25-Oct 1, 2026 (week_label shows Sep 24-Oct 1 for continuity). GBP Posts Published for this window verified via getScheduledPosts (ground-truth local publicationDate + status per property's own timezone): 3 properties published a real GBP post inside this window (Residences at the Overlook, Santa Fe, Villa Siena -- all Fri Sep 25 local); everyone else's next post is scheduled for Fri Oct 2 and still PENDING, not yet live. GBP WINDOW: re-ran the walk-back completeness test (GMEV18/reachSearch non-null for all 7 days, every GBP-connected property) starting from this run's own week -- Sep 25-Oct 1 failed (only 1 of 7 days present), and Sep 18-24 and Sep 11-17 both failed again too (1 of 7 and 3 of 7 days respectively, Sep 11-17 unchanged for three weeks running now), so the window falls back to GBP_CURRENT = Sep 4-10 (Sep 3-10, 2026) / GBP_PRIOR = Aug 28-Sep 3 (Aug 27-Sep 3, 2026) -- unchanged for the third week running. Spot-checked GMEV18 for Sep 4-10 across multiple properties and confirmed digit-for-digit identical to the last two runs' fully-verified pulls, so google_business/gbp_by_property/gbp_window are carried over verbatim again this run rather than re-pulling all five fields for all 13 properties a third time. Engagement KPI = social interactions (Facebook 1 + Instagram 38 + TikTok 682 = 721) + GBP action clicks (1,695, same GBP_CURRENT window as above) = 2,416, per the 2026-09-12 methodology; delta computed straight against last week's published Engagement (2,558) -- note this is a real drop in social interactions week over week, not a data issue (GBP clicks are flat since the window didn't move). Facebook Groups metrics stay at 0/0 (still manual-only, unchanged). URL Tracking and GMB URL Tracking: no new GA4 export received this week -- both carried forward unchanged from the last real numbers (delta 0) rather than disappearing, per policy. views_by_channel computed fresh this run (Facebook 807 + Instagram 6,937 + TikTok 12,120 + Google Business 0 = 19,864, matches kpis.views). MANUAL CORRECTION (2026-10-03, per Val): Ingleside Terrace published a GBP post on Sep 30, 2026 directly through the Google Business Profile app, bypassing Metricool's scheduler entirely -- getScheduledPosts cannot see it (it only lists posts Metricool itself scheduled), and the lone gmb-network entry it returned for this property (id 385337536) is an unrelated, still-PENDING post queued for Oct 2. Val confirmed the Sep 30 post directly, so it is added by hand: Ingleside Terrace posts_channels[\"Google Business\"] 0 -> 1, posts.current 3 -> 4; posts_by_channel Google Business 3 -> 4; kpis.posts.current 42 -> 43, delta -1 -> 0. This does NOT touch google_business / gbp_by_property / gbp_window (the GBP_CURRENT rollup section) -- that window is Sep 4-10, unaffected by a Sep 30 post. Once GMEV17 (the evolution connector's postsCount field, which reads Google's own account activity regardless of origin) finishes syncing for this window -- currently only 1 of 7 days present -- it should corroborate this post independently; if it does not, that is worth a second look. URL TRACKING UPDATE (2026-10-03): Val shared this week's real GA4 export for both FB Groups and GMB link tracking (window Sep 24-Oct 2, 2026). FB Groups: Views 44, Sessions 23, Engaged Sessions 15, Tours 0 (delta vs last real reading Sep 17-25: -41/-7/-3/0). GMB: Views 1,344, Sessions 388, Engaged Sessions 261, Key Events 0 (delta vs last real reading Sep 17-25: +37/-77/-23/0). Both replace the carried-forward placeholders this file originally shipped with.\n\nCORRECTION (2026-10-08): Val flagged that Metricool's own UI showed September GBP data fully loaded (only the standard 5-6 day disclaimer), contradicting this report's GBP window falling back to Sep 4-10 for three weeks running. Investigated and found the real cause: requesting all 5 GBP evolution fields (GMEV18/19/21/22/23) together in one getAnalyticsDataByMetrics call intermittently drops dates from the merged result -- confirmed by re-running the identical 5-field query twice, seconds apart, on the same property: the first call cut off partway through the month, the second returned the full range cleanly. This was never a real multi-week Metricool/Google sync lag. Re-ran the walk-back completeness check fresh (still pulling all 5 fields together, but this time verifying each property returns exactly 7 rows and retrying any that don't) for this run's own week (Sep 25-Oct 1) and the prior week (Sep 18-24): both came back fully complete on first/retry attempt, all 13 GBP-connected properties, no gaps. GBP_CURRENT/GBP_PRIOR are therefore corrected to Sep 25-Oct 1 / Sep 18-24 -- the report's own current and prior weeks, exactly as they should be when GBP isn't actually lagging. google_business, gbp_by_property, gbp_window(_label), and the Google Business component of Engagement are all recomputed against this corrected window; posts_published/posts_by_channel were already correct since those come from getScheduledPosts ground truth, not the affected evolution connector. Engagement's delta is still computed against the Engagement figure actually published last week (2,558), consistent with how every other KPI's delta works here -- not a retroactive recomputation of last week's own (possibly similarly affected) GBP numbers, which were not revisited. AUTOMATION.md updated with the root cause and a revised, more reliable completeness-check procedure going forward.",
